nelsonm@ctron.com (Matt Nelson) writes:
>   I've successfully compiled nethack 3.1.3 with X windows on an SGI Indigo
> running IRIX 5.2 (SysVr4, X11R5). I've encountered only one problem; When
> I run nethack I get the message:
> 
> Warning: Cannot convert string "nh10" to type FontStruct
> 
>   I have no problems with nethack 3.1.3 on an Indigo running IRIX 4.0.5. I
> can't find the above message in the nethack source, so I would guess that
> it's an X11R4/R5 problem, but that's all it is: a guess.
> 
>   Does anyone have any suggestions on fixing this?

Simply don't use the nh10 font. Add the line

NetHack*map*font:                       *-lucidatypewriter-bold-*-14-*

or some such to your X defaults file. It should be a proportional font,
(all chars the same size) i.e courier is ok but times and helvetica
are not.

